Seraphim wrote:
> As far as I'm aware [Google Groups] doesn't have a "find parent" function...

This is only technically true. The deeper truth, as I'm sure you know,
is that the parent-child relationship is constructed out of the
References: header, which contains a list of message IDs; Google makes
the References header readily available to you, and makes it
straightforward to search for an article by messageID. It remains for
somebody to package these two functions into a one-click "find parent"
addin (firefox extension, greasemonkey script, what have you).

Incidentally, it has been often true in the past that newsreaders --
particularly Outlook Express -- have been pilloried precisely because
they *don't* respect or even properly construct the References: header.
 Google Groups and its predecessor Deja News *always* have and always
will handle this header properly.

